# --- riscv64, measured 2026-07-28, when the body classifier first became able
# --- to see RISC-V at all. Before this the classifier knew only x86-64 and
# --- aarch64 mnemonics, scored 0 of 4 on a probe of unambiguous RISC-V fakes,
# --- and the rv32/rv64 link sites therefore carried NO guard call
# --- (doc/08_tracking/bug/simpleos_fabricated_rt_guard_riscv_classifier_inert_2026-07-28.md).
# --- It now scores 4 of 4, and 11 of 11 against the stub source that
# --- link_simpleos_riscv64 generates. Both disassemblers agree exactly.
#
# --- PROVENANCE / CAVEAT -- read before trusting or extending these rows.
# --- These were NOT taken from a completed pure-Simple link. The deployed
# --- bin/simple is currently the Rust bootstrap seed, whose own Rust linker
# --- handles freestanding links, so link_simpleos_riscv64 is not reachable
# --- end-to-end from the CLI today and no live per-entry run could be made.
# --- What WAS measured, with the code's own algorithm and flags:
# ---   trivial = the 11 constant-return rt_* in the stub source generated by
# ---     link_simpleos_riscv64, compiled with that function's exact flags
# ---     (riscv64-unknown-elf-gcc -c -march=rv64gc -mabi=lp64d -ffreestanding
# ---     -nostdlib -- note NO -O, which is why the bodies carry a full frame).
# ---   refs = nm -u over the user objects of the riscv64 smoke_entry closure
# ---     (--target riscv64-unknown-none, --emit-archive, 1 module).
# ---   channel 2 = trivial INTERSECT refs = the five rows below.
# --- Channel 1 was deliberately NOT baselined: on this entry it reports ~55
# --- core runtime symbols (rt_alloc, rt_array_*, rt_string_*, ...) that
# --- link_simpleos_riscv64 supplies from no object at all -- it links only
# --- entry_o + user objects + stub_o + init_o. That is an unlinkable
# --- configuration, not debt, and writing 55 rows here would launder a broken
# --- route into a baseline. Fix the route, then measure channel 1.
# --- The six other trivial stub symbols (rt_riscv_qemu_ram_base / _ram_size /
# --- _reserved_end / _heap_start / _heap_size, rt_riscv_noalloc_pmm_init) are
# --- NOT referenced by this entry and so are deliberately absent. The five
# --- memory-map accessors among them are legitimate constant returns and need
# --- a per-symbol rationale when an entry that does reference them is measured
# --- -- do not blanket-add them.
# --- Every other riscv entry (simpleos_riscv64_display_smoke.elf,
# --- _host_gpu_probe.elf, _fpga.elf, _desktop_service.elf, and every riscv32
# --- entry) carries NO rows and is therefore maximally strict. riscv32 could
# --- not be measured at all: its closure needs --backend llvm (cranelift
# --- refuses hosted riscv32).
simpleos_riscv64_smf_fs.elf rt_riscv_native_gui_process_render
simpleos_riscv64_smf_fs.elf rt_riscv_nvfs_probe
simpleos_riscv64_smf_fs.elf rt_riscv_smf_cli_load
simpleos_riscv64_smf_fs.elf rt_riscv_smf_cli_probe
simpleos_riscv64_smf_fs.elf rt_riscv_smf_gui_probe
